# Architecture

Keep frontend and backend separated under `frontend/` and `backend/`.

## Local stack

- Frontend: React + Vite + TypeScript.
- Backend: AWS SAM CLI, TypeScript Lambda handlers.
- Local AWS substitutes: LocalStack for DynamoDB and S3, Docker Compose. OpenSearch in Docker later.

## Future shipping target (do not implement unless asked)

AWS Lambda, API Gateway, DynamoDB, S3, Cognito, OpenSearch, EventBridge, Amplify Hosting.

## Data and identity

- DynamoDB is the source of truth. OpenSearch is a derived search index only, never the source of truth.
- Scope every data access by `userId`. Never query or write across users.
- Local auth may use a demo identity only behind an auth adapter. Production auth must stay Cognito-compatible (adapter interface now; no Cognito wiring unless requested).

```typescript
// ❌ BAD — unscoped access / OpenSearch as system of record
await table.scan({});
await index.getInvoice(id); // treating search as source of truth

// ✅ GOOD
await table.query({ userId, invoiceId });
await dynamo.getInvoice({ userId, invoiceId });
```
